{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "טפכם", :translit "tapkhem", :gloss "your little ones"} {:he "בעיני הראשים לנהלם ולהדריכם כטפם", :translit "b'einei ha-rashim l'nahalam ul'hadrikhem k'tapam", :gloss "in the eyes of the leaders to guide them and lead them like their little ones"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Wordplay: the same term טפ (little ones) applied to the nation instructs leaders how to treat the people — as one's own children."}], :frame {:text "Deuteronomy 29:9 instructs the heads of tribes and elders to assemble the people; the juxtaposition of ראשיכם שטריכם זקניכם (your heads, your officers, your elders) at the start of the list frames the leaders' role. The Talmud teaches that one must be careful regarding the honor due to students, as implied by the phrase שבטך ומשענתך (your staff and your support) which is read as referring to students (Sanhedrin 5b); and that a leader must bear the community as a nurse carries a suckling, per the verse וְאֶתְכֶם יִשָּׂא ... כַּאֲשֶׁר יִשָּׂא הָאֹמֵן אֶת־הַיָּנֵק (Numbers 11:12).", :sources ["Sanhedrin 5b" "Numbers 11:12" "Deuteronomy 29:9"]}} {:quotes [{:he "נשיכם", :translit "nashekhem", :gloss "your women"} {:he "וגרך", :translit "v'gerkha", :gloss "and your stranger"} {:he "להנשא לפסולין", :translit "l'henasei li-f'sulin", :gloss "to marry those disqualified"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Adjacent-words (סמוכים) hint: נשיכם followed immediately by וגרך signals that women may marry those outside the permitted circle."}], :frame {:text "The verse lists נשיך וטפך וגרך אשר בקרב מחניך (your women, your little ones, and your stranger who is in your camp) — all standing together to enter the covenant. The Talmud (Yevamot 47a) addresses laws of marriage with converts and their disqualified relatives. The Mekhilta (Nezikin 3) interprets גר as a definite term indicating a full convert; and the Sifrei on Deuteronomy 29:11 categorizes each group listed in the verse as parties to the covenant.", :sources ["Yevamot 47a" "Mekhilta Nezikin 3" "Sifrei Deuteronomy 29:11" "Deuteronomy 29:10"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Wordplay: the same term טפ (little ones) applied to the nation instructs leaders how to treat the people — as one's own children.", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :other, :note "Adjacent-words (סמוכים) hint: נשיכם followed immediately by וגרך signals that women may marry those outside the permitted circle.", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:40:19.299248855Z", :model "glm-5.2"}